randomChainComplex -- random chain complex over the integers with prescribed ranks of the homology group and ranks of the matrices
**********************************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        C = randomChainComplex(h,r)
  * Inputs:
      * h, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of desired ranks of the homology
        groups, of some length $n$
      * r, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of desired ranks of the matrices
        in the complex, of length $n-1$
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Height => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value 10, the
        sizes of the random integers used
      * WithLLL => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value
        true, use the LLL algorithm to keep the sizes of the integers small
      * ZeroMean => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default
        value true, whether to balance the random numbers around zero
  * Outputs:
      * C, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, a random chain complex over
        the integers whose homology ranks match $h$, and whose matrices have
        ranks given by $r$

Description
===========





+------------------------------------------+
|i1 : h={1,4,6,5,1}                        |
|                                          |
|o1 = {1, 4, 6, 5, 1}                      |
|                                          |
|o1 : List                                 |
+------------------------------------------+
|i2 : r={1,3,3,4}                          |
|                                          |
|o2 = {1, 3, 3, 4}                         |
|                                          |
|o2 : List                                 |
+------------------------------------------+
|i3 : C=randomChainComplex(h,r)            |
|                                          |
|       2       8       12       12       5|
|o3 = ZZ  <-- ZZ  <-- ZZ   <-- ZZ   <-- ZZ |
|                                          |
|     0       1       2        3        4  |
|                                          |
|o3 : Complex                              |
+------------------------------------------+
|i4 : prune HH C                           |
|                                          |
|       1       4       6       5       1  |
|o4 = ZZ  <-- ZZ  <-- ZZ  <-- ZZ  <-- ZZ   |
|                                          |
|     0       1       2       3       4    |
|                                          |
|o4 : Complex                              |
+------------------------------------------+
|i5 : for i from 0 to 4 list rank HH_i C   |
|                                          |
|o5 = {1, 4, 6, 5, 1}                      |
|                                          |
|o5 : List                                 |
+------------------------------------------+
|i6 : for i from 1 to 4 list rank(C.dd_i)  |
|                                          |
|o6 = {1, 3, 3, 4}                         |
|                                          |
|o6 : List                                 |
+------------------------------------------+

The optional argument Height chooses the maximum sizes of the random numbers
used. The actual numbers are somewhat larger (twice as many bits), as matrices
are multiplied together.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : h={1,4,0,5,1}                                                           |
